IMPORT policy

-- Standing preamble (applied to every query below): "Assuming all other conditions are met
-- and no other exclusions apply", and the agreement is signed and the premium paid on time.
-- Fields unrelated to a given question are set to baseline values under which every
-- condition for coverage is satisfied and no exclusion is triggered:
--   `agreement signed` = TRUE, `premium paid month` = JUST 0, `policy term months` = 12,
--   wellness-visit facts fully compliant (visit before month 6, confirmation before month 7,
--   qualified provider), no fraud/misrepresentation, no dispute (so the arbitration and
--   60-day-recovery sub-clauses are vacuously satisfied), `causes` = EMPTY, and an
--   `age at hospitalization` well under 80.
-- See NOTES.md for the judgement calls behind the field choices below.

§ `Q1 -- burns suffered while on duty as a firefighter`

q1 MEANS Claim WITH
    `agreement signed`                        IS TRUE
    `premium paid month`                      IS JUST 0
    `hospitalization month`                   IS 1
    `hospitalization ground`                  IS `Accidental injury`
    `age at hospitalization`                  IS 40
    causes                                    IS LIST Firefighting
    `fraud month`                             IS NOTHING
    `misrepresentation month`                 IS NOTHING
    `wellness visit month`                    IS JUST 3
    `wellness visit provider qualified`       IS TRUE
    `written confirmation month`              IS JUST 5
    `dispute arisen`                          IS FALSE
    `unable to settle month`                  IS NOTHING
    `arbitration commenced month`             IS NOTHING
    `valid arbitration award issued`          IS TRUE
    `written proof of claim month`            IS NOTHING
    `recovery sought month`                   IS NOTHING
    `policy term months`                      IS 12

#EVAL covered q1

